<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Custoza (1848)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1848">1848</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-italian-war-of-independence">First Italian War of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Custoza was fought on 24–25 July 1848 near Verona during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-italian-war-of-independence">First Italian War of Independence</a>, between the Austrian army of Field Marshal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-radetzky-von-radetz">Joseph Radetzky</a> and the Sardinian army of King Charles Albert. The Austrian victory forced the Piedmontese to withdraw from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a> and accept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> of Salasco. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> reoccupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, although <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> held out until August 1849.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-custoza-1848.jpg" alt="Battle of Custoza (1848)" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Felice Cerruti Bauduc (1817-1896) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sommacampagna_1848.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the Risorgimento the army, including the Bersaglieri light infantry created in 1836, was beaten by Austria at <b>Custoza</b> in 1848 and Novara in 1849.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-sardinia">Kingdom of Sardinia · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>After the Piedmontese defeat at <b>Custoza</b> in July 1848, Radetzky reoccupied Milan on 6 August, and Lombardy returned to the Kingdom of Lombardy-Venetia.</blockquote><a href="/state/provisional-government-of-milan">Provisional Government of Milan</a></li><li><blockquote>The republic briefly voted in July 1848 to join the Kingdom of Sardinia, but after Piedmont's defeat at <b>Custoza</b> it returned to independence.</blockquote><a href="/state/republic-of-san-marco">Republic of San Marco</a></li></ul></section>
